WEBVTT

00:22.708 --> 00:26.041
ACROBATIC SHOW
FEMALE KNIFE THROWER

00:29.166 --> 00:31.041
Stop doing that and pour me a drink!

00:31.125 --> 00:32.416
-That's right!
-Yeah!

00:32.500 --> 00:34.416
How long are you gonna keep
throwing those?

00:34.500 --> 00:36.208
Come here and drink with us!

00:36.291 --> 00:40.083
Nobody throws knives anymore anyway!

00:40.166 --> 00:41.875
You've got a pretty face.

00:41.958 --> 00:44.208
Take your clothes off and sing for us!

00:44.291 --> 00:45.166
Damn right!

00:45.250 --> 00:49.125
Show us your beautiful fair skin.
Pretty please!

00:54.125 --> 00:57.666
CIVILIZATION AND ENLIGHTENMENT

00:57.750 --> 00:58.833
Bravo!

00:59.500 --> 01:01.458
That's impressive!

01:03.041 --> 01:05.458
-I want a big one.
-Me too.

01:05.541 --> 01:07.541
I can't deal with this without good food.

01:07.625 --> 01:09.333
Can you raise my pay?

01:09.416 --> 01:12.000
The customers don't like it,
so stop your whining.

01:13.125 --> 01:14.500
Iroha.

01:14.583 --> 01:18.041
Why don't you sell those knives instead,
or start selling your body?

01:18.875 --> 01:21.458
I don't mind paying for it.

01:24.250 --> 01:26.500
What? What's that face for?

01:27.625 --> 01:28.583
Huh?

01:30.500 --> 01:33.375
Have you forgotten who took you in?

01:33.458 --> 01:34.666
I'm talking to you.

01:40.041 --> 01:41.416
So you were alive.

01:43.041 --> 01:44.125
I'm glad.

01:45.958 --> 01:48.500
I didn't expect you
to be a traveling entertainer.

01:48.583 --> 01:50.291
It was hard to find you.

01:50.791 --> 01:52.750
I'm surprised you didn't get angry.

01:52.833 --> 01:56.083
The old Iroha
would've slashed them all to death.

01:57.083 --> 01:58.291
I'm used to it.

02:00.000 --> 02:01.208
What about you, Sansuke?

02:01.750 --> 02:02.625
Well.

02:03.125 --> 02:07.041
I'm pulling a rickshaw every day
to feed my wife and daughter.

02:07.916 --> 02:10.916
I see. You have a family now.

02:11.000 --> 02:11.833
Yes.

02:12.333 --> 02:15.291
And you? What did you do
after you left the mountain?

02:18.583 --> 02:19.666
Many things.

02:20.458 --> 02:23.166
I moved from place to place,
hiding from Gentosai.

02:27.458 --> 02:28.708
And the others?

02:43.750 --> 02:46.416
Fugoro and Shichiya
were killed by Gentosai.

02:48.791 --> 02:51.625
He's been searching
for the surviving Kyohachi-ryu.

02:54.375 --> 02:55.250
Iroha.

02:56.041 --> 02:58.375
If we don't do something,
both of us will be killed.

02:59.666 --> 03:02.250
I already found Shikura and Jinroku
and convinced them.

03:02.333 --> 03:03.750
They're in the army now.

03:06.125 --> 03:08.125
What are you trying to do?

03:13.250 --> 03:16.416
We'll use this to draw Gentosai out
and kill him ourselves.

03:16.500 --> 03:19.708
Unless all of us attack together,
we won't be able to kill him.

03:21.041 --> 03:22.000
Iroha.

03:24.708 --> 03:26.916
This is our fate.

03:47.500 --> 03:48.958
Sorry to keep you waiting.

03:49.625 --> 03:53.958
And now, to discover
the true identity of Kodoku,

03:54.041 --> 03:55.958
it's time for
the great strategist Kyojin--

03:56.041 --> 03:58.083
Just get to the point.

04:01.000 --> 04:02.958
We're running two experiments.

04:03.041 --> 04:04.750
For the first one,

04:05.250 --> 04:09.000
we'll hand over a participant
with a wooden tag to the police.

04:11.333 --> 04:14.125
Once detained, they'll be held there
until the end of the game.

04:14.208 --> 04:15.916
They're basically out of the game.

04:16.000 --> 04:20.625
Normally, you can't
kill someone who's in jail.

04:20.708 --> 04:24.541
So the question is whether Kodoku
would still make a move?

04:24.625 --> 04:25.666
Correct.

04:25.750 --> 04:29.083
Whether they would defy authority
to silence someone,

04:29.166 --> 04:32.250
or at least stop short
of interfering with the police…

04:32.833 --> 04:35.916
This will show us how far
the Kodoku organizer is willing to go.

04:38.625 --> 04:40.458
And for the second one,

04:41.041 --> 04:43.875
we'll find out
where the dead bodies disappear to.

04:44.666 --> 04:46.125
-Disappear?
-Yes.

04:46.791 --> 04:50.791
Dozens of people are killing each other
along the Tokaido Road.

04:51.375 --> 04:55.666
Surely there should be a dead body or two
lying there on the side of the road.

04:55.750 --> 04:56.833
However…

04:58.375 --> 05:01.375
We haven't seen any dead bodies
that were killed in battle.

05:01.458 --> 05:02.791
Exactly.

05:06.833 --> 05:11.083
You know that the Kodoku
are monitoring the participants?

05:14.166 --> 05:17.416
Well, they won't follow us inside.

05:18.000 --> 05:20.291
But the Kodoku are watching us.

05:21.125 --> 05:24.833
So they're the ones
who dispose of the dead bodies?

05:24.916 --> 05:27.791
Yes. They must be taking them somewhere.

05:28.458 --> 05:29.625
Which means?

05:30.708 --> 05:32.375
They have manpower and hiding spots

05:32.458 --> 05:36.041
to dispose of bodies across different
locations without getting caught.

05:36.125 --> 05:37.666
Excellent answer.

05:38.208 --> 05:40.333
If we can find
where the dead bodies are taken,

05:40.416 --> 05:43.041
maybe we can figure out
who is behind this game.

05:44.541 --> 05:47.041
So? I'm quite a strategist, right?

05:50.708 --> 05:53.416
So? Where do we start?

05:53.916 --> 05:57.291
First, we hunt for a candidate
to hand over to the police.

06:30.500 --> 06:33.875
Why would the zaibatsu
procure over 100 rifles

06:33.958 --> 06:35.958
and make the shizoku kill each other?

06:36.458 --> 06:37.791
Since the Meiji era started,

06:37.875 --> 06:40.333
they've made a fortune
through government work.

06:41.958 --> 06:44.666
What do they possibly gain
from doing something like this?

06:46.000 --> 06:49.833
Using money as bait
to force the shizoku to kill each other…

06:51.083 --> 06:53.916
Couldn't it be that their slaughter
is the very goal itself?

06:58.291 --> 07:00.708
A grudge against the shizoku.

07:01.208 --> 07:05.125
They have long been tormented
by the shizoku's unreasonable extortion.

07:05.208 --> 07:07.625
According to the zaibatsu,

07:07.708 --> 07:12.625
the four in question
have been on leave since a week ago.

07:13.125 --> 07:16.583
No one knows their whereabouts,
and they're not at their homes.

07:17.541 --> 07:19.041
Find them immediately.

07:19.125 --> 07:19.958
Yes, sir.

07:20.458 --> 07:21.708
Lord Okubo, if I may,

07:21.791 --> 07:25.916
taking action against the zaibatsu
could affect our nation's economy--

07:26.000 --> 07:27.166
Shinpei.

07:27.250 --> 07:29.541
If they're the ones
pulling the strings behind this,

07:29.625 --> 07:31.500
it will be considered high treason.

07:32.916 --> 07:35.250
We must deal with this at once.

07:36.666 --> 07:37.958
-Kawaji.
-Yes, sir?

07:38.041 --> 07:40.125
I want you to bring them here.

07:40.208 --> 07:42.875
I will locate their whereabouts
as soon as possible.

07:43.958 --> 07:46.250
-I'll start analyzing the telegrams.
-Yes.

07:57.500 --> 07:58.916
KUWANA-JUKU

07:59.000 --> 08:00.250
Come, come!

08:00.333 --> 08:02.375
Grilled clams, Kuwana's specialty!

08:02.458 --> 08:04.541
Come and get your grilled clams!

08:04.625 --> 08:09.708
We've got horse mackerels, clams,
bigfin reef squid, and delicious sake too!

08:10.208 --> 08:11.708
You must be tired from traveling.

08:11.791 --> 08:13.833
Would you like to take a short break here?

08:13.916 --> 08:15.458
Thank you very much.

08:15.541 --> 08:17.541
Customers coming in!

08:18.375 --> 08:22.416
Welcome! A group of four coming in!

08:30.750 --> 08:34.291
Please go ahead!
We have a table in the back!

08:35.541 --> 08:37.916
Miss, fetch us some tea and skewers.

08:38.416 --> 08:40.833
Tea and four plates of skewers!

08:44.166 --> 08:46.958
Okay, one bowl of mixed rice!

08:47.958 --> 08:49.958
One flying squid!

08:55.791 --> 08:56.916
Look at that guy.

08:58.500 --> 09:01.458
He's not even hiding his wooden tag.
That's some confidence.

09:05.250 --> 09:06.750
They're participants too.

09:07.458 --> 09:08.916
I saw them at Tenryuji Temple.

09:11.458 --> 09:12.875
Which one should we go for?

09:12.958 --> 09:14.625
Don't mess me around!

09:14.708 --> 09:15.541
I'm sorry!

09:15.625 --> 09:17.291
Useless, clumsy idiot!

09:17.375 --> 09:19.416
I'm really sorry! I'm sorry!

09:19.500 --> 09:20.791
Shut it!

09:20.875 --> 09:21.958
I'm sorry…

09:22.041 --> 09:23.916
Let's go with whoever leaves first.

09:27.500 --> 09:30.041
That won't be necessary.

09:35.416 --> 09:36.291
Who are you?

09:43.833 --> 09:45.875
So there was one more than I thought.

09:46.375 --> 09:48.416
"One more"? Hmm?

09:48.916 --> 09:50.833
What exactly do you mean?

09:53.333 --> 09:54.333
Huh?

10:04.291 --> 10:07.916
Most participants pass by this teahouse.

10:08.416 --> 10:12.416
So I took the liberty of setting a trap.

10:12.500 --> 10:15.666
Isn't it a violation of the rules to
tell non-participants about this?

10:15.750 --> 10:18.833
It's not a violation if I hire them
without giving them the details.

10:18.916 --> 10:20.583
So much for a strategist.

10:20.666 --> 10:22.250
This is nothing.

10:25.708 --> 10:26.708
As for the girls…

10:28.541 --> 10:31.666
Do as you please with them.

10:40.208 --> 10:43.416
Okay, carry on.

10:54.875 --> 10:55.958
YOKKAICHI-JUKU

10:56.041 --> 10:58.750
Yokkaichi's known for Banko ceramics!

10:58.833 --> 11:00.291
Come take a look!

11:07.500 --> 11:09.250
Lower-intermediate.

11:12.458 --> 11:13.833
A beginner.

11:19.000 --> 11:20.625
Pre-intermediate.

11:38.875 --> 11:39.791
Hey, you.

11:41.208 --> 11:42.958
You're a participant, aren't you?

11:44.250 --> 11:47.166
Have you seen a guy with a girl in tow?

11:48.625 --> 11:49.625
No.

11:51.125 --> 11:52.083
Goddammit.

11:52.958 --> 11:56.291
After years of waiting,
this is what I get?

12:00.583 --> 12:01.625
A bow, huh?

12:02.291 --> 12:05.958
What's fun about shooting arrows
here and there from so far away?

12:06.541 --> 12:08.791
It's no different from a gun.

12:10.875 --> 12:13.750
This tool is used
to make offerings to the gods.

12:14.500 --> 12:15.583
It does not compare.

12:38.666 --> 12:40.791
To hell with the gods.

12:41.666 --> 12:43.041
What a joke.

12:43.125 --> 12:45.125
My dear!

12:45.708 --> 12:49.000
Oh no! Open your eyes, please!

12:49.083 --> 12:52.708
You monster… Please! Wake up…

12:56.875 --> 13:02.958
If gods were real…
the world would be different.

13:20.708 --> 13:21.583
Good.

13:26.041 --> 13:27.416
Let's play.

13:39.375 --> 13:41.083
Die, you bastard!

13:44.791 --> 13:46.750
Girls! Go for the girls!

13:46.833 --> 13:49.708
If you take their wooden tags,
I'll triple the pay!

14:20.250 --> 14:21.458
Move!

14:25.083 --> 14:27.125
Look who's caught now?

14:29.208 --> 14:31.333
What the hell's going on?

14:31.416 --> 14:32.833
This isn't what we were told!

14:32.916 --> 14:34.625
You can't leave. I'm paying you!

14:37.791 --> 14:38.708
Hey!

15:05.916 --> 15:08.875
Go! Hurry the hell up!

15:22.791 --> 15:24.958
Come on, go!

15:51.416 --> 15:53.000
Die!

16:14.583 --> 16:16.916
Someone! Go get the police!

16:18.250 --> 16:19.500
Out of the way!

16:51.958 --> 16:54.750
It's an offering to the gods.

17:10.625 --> 17:11.791
That's enough.

17:19.458 --> 17:21.375
Do I know you from somewhere?

17:21.458 --> 17:23.666
The police are on their way here.

17:23.750 --> 17:24.708
Yeah?

17:24.791 --> 17:26.208
So what?

17:26.291 --> 17:29.208
Those on the organizer's side
have high expectations for you two.

17:29.291 --> 17:31.375
Having you eliminated will spoil the game.

17:31.458 --> 17:33.541
You think I'll get caught?

17:34.416 --> 17:37.583
I can go ahead and cut you down here.

17:38.166 --> 17:39.583
Be my guest.

17:40.791 --> 17:43.750
If you think you can win
against this many rifles.

17:49.583 --> 17:50.916
I've lost interest.

18:00.416 --> 18:02.291
The times have changed.

18:02.375 --> 18:04.333
There's no place left
for the samurai to live.

18:06.125 --> 18:10.500
You went through hell
after the war, didn't you?

18:13.166 --> 18:14.916
Bukotsu Kanjiya?

18:17.666 --> 18:20.125
It's none of your damn business.

18:50.916 --> 18:53.583
All right, then. Which one is it gonna be?

18:54.333 --> 18:58.000
What are you going to make us do?

18:58.083 --> 19:02.250
We're going to give one of you
to the police with your wooden tag.

19:02.833 --> 19:03.666
What?

19:05.208 --> 19:07.125
What? Wait a second…

19:07.750 --> 19:08.791
If you do that--

19:08.875 --> 19:12.083
Kodoku will kill you,
or the police will protect you.

19:12.166 --> 19:13.416
One or the other.

19:13.958 --> 19:14.791
What?

19:15.791 --> 19:17.916
And the one who isn't given to the police?

19:18.000 --> 19:20.333
We grab his wooden tag,
and he drops out right here.

19:23.166 --> 19:24.791
Hand me over to the police!

19:25.833 --> 19:27.000
I-I'll go!

19:27.083 --> 19:28.083
What?

19:28.166 --> 19:31.083
I'm the one who's going.
You keep your mouth shut!

19:33.583 --> 19:36.166
Well, I'm afraid you're
dropping out here, young man.

19:40.375 --> 19:43.000
Please. I'll do anything!

19:43.083 --> 19:46.500
Just accept it.
You've killed plenty already too.

19:46.583 --> 19:48.375
I haven't killed anyone at all!

19:48.458 --> 19:51.541
Even at Tenryuji Temple,
I just picked up a tag someone dropped.

19:51.625 --> 19:53.083
I'm sure… No lies, please.

19:53.166 --> 19:54.500
I'm not lying!

19:56.083 --> 19:58.708
This man threatened me.

20:00.000 --> 20:02.041
He told me he'd at least keep me alive.

20:02.125 --> 20:03.625
Stop lying!

20:07.166 --> 20:08.750
I come from a poor family.

20:09.916 --> 20:12.500
I joined because I wanted
to help my father's business.

20:16.541 --> 20:18.000
But then…

20:20.750 --> 20:22.416
It was a killing game…

20:25.791 --> 20:27.458
and I just couldn't do it.

20:31.916 --> 20:32.750
I'm begging you.

20:35.083 --> 20:38.791
Please… Please spare my life!

20:45.625 --> 20:47.333
You heard what he said.

20:55.750 --> 20:57.541
I guess you win.

20:59.541 --> 21:03.375
But you're gonna
lend me a hand in return, okay?

21:06.833 --> 21:08.333
Thank you.

21:10.958 --> 21:12.625
Thank you!

21:13.916 --> 21:14.750
What?

21:15.250 --> 21:16.583
Wait a minute.

21:16.666 --> 21:17.750
I can help you out too--

21:17.833 --> 21:21.000
Shujiro, you guys go and check
where the dead bodies are being taken.

21:21.083 --> 21:21.916
Okay.

21:22.500 --> 21:24.166
Oh, and you, Iroha.

21:25.000 --> 21:25.833
Here.

21:27.833 --> 21:28.875
What's this?

21:28.958 --> 21:30.291
It's a smoke ball.

21:30.375 --> 21:32.333
I don't need this.

21:32.416 --> 21:33.750
Just keep it with you.

21:34.333 --> 21:36.375
I'll call the police here.

21:36.458 --> 21:41.333
Use the commotion
to shake off the Kodoku watchers first.

21:41.875 --> 21:42.958
All right!

21:43.750 --> 21:46.875
Let's get this mission underway.

21:54.041 --> 21:54.875
Come in.

21:58.625 --> 22:00.125
The analysis results came out.

22:00.208 --> 22:04.291
Just as you suspected,
they're communicating by telegram.

22:04.375 --> 22:06.875
DOMESTIC TELEGRAM RECORD

22:06.958 --> 22:10.291
Since May 5th, the day of
the reported incident at Tenryuji Temple,

22:10.375 --> 22:13.375
telegram correspondence
has drastically increased.

22:13.458 --> 22:15.375
NUMBER OF TELEGRAMS
MAY 5TH: 156

22:15.458 --> 22:16.541
What else?

22:16.625 --> 22:18.625
We can't figure out the content

22:18.708 --> 22:21.083
since they're corresponding in code.

22:25.333 --> 22:26.166
However,

22:26.750 --> 22:29.083
we did find out
where these telegrams originated.

22:30.291 --> 22:31.125
Where?

22:31.708 --> 22:33.250
-Show him the map.
-Yes, sir.

22:39.875 --> 22:42.041
The southern foot of Mount Fuji.

22:43.750 --> 22:46.791
The map suggests there's nothing there.

22:46.875 --> 22:48.291
MOUNT FUJI
SHIZUOKA TELEGRAPH OFFICE

22:48.916 --> 22:51.083
The zaibatsu's stronghold.

22:52.166 --> 22:54.291
Kawaji. Head there immediately.

23:04.750 --> 23:10.333
"Clash between shizoku
in Yokkaichi City on Tokaido Road…"

23:24.458 --> 23:25.458
Gentlemen.

23:26.416 --> 23:27.291
What is it?

23:27.791 --> 23:29.541
The government is taking action.

23:29.625 --> 23:30.458
What?

23:32.708 --> 23:34.416
I wouldn't worry about it.

23:34.916 --> 23:37.916
There is no way they can reach us here.

23:38.958 --> 23:42.750
We have a guardian angel
on our side, after all.

23:46.750 --> 23:49.250
Oh, yes. You're right about that.

23:50.250 --> 23:51.208
Well said.

23:57.708 --> 24:00.375
Thank you for earlier.

24:03.875 --> 24:07.458
How old were you
when you started training, Iroha?

24:11.083 --> 24:13.583
All of the Kyohachi-ryu
were abandoned as children.

24:14.083 --> 24:15.750
We don't know our real ages.

24:16.333 --> 24:19.208
Were there any other girls?

24:20.875 --> 24:21.791
No.

24:23.541 --> 24:25.083
I was young

24:26.500 --> 24:27.958
and the weakest of them all.

24:28.541 --> 24:29.750
You were the weakest?

24:31.125 --> 24:32.583
It was a long time ago.

24:46.583 --> 24:50.666
What should I do to be as strong as you?

24:59.625 --> 25:01.250
You don't have to…

25:02.625 --> 25:04.250
and there's no need.

25:07.083 --> 25:09.291
No matter how skilled
you get at using a sword…

25:11.750 --> 25:13.375
it won't bring you happiness.

25:19.458 --> 25:20.333
He's here.

25:33.000 --> 25:35.541
Ow! That hurts.

25:36.041 --> 25:38.416
No need to be so rough!

25:39.208 --> 25:40.708
H-Hello, sir.

25:41.208 --> 25:43.083
He's the suspect for the teahouse murders.

25:43.166 --> 25:44.125
You've got it wrong.

25:44.208 --> 25:45.833
We'll hold him in jail.

25:45.916 --> 25:46.750
Yes, sir.

25:46.833 --> 25:48.375
-Let's go!
-Ow, ow!

25:55.583 --> 25:57.916
I can't wait to see what happens.

25:59.583 --> 26:01.375
-No!
-Silence!

26:01.458 --> 26:02.500
POLICE BRANCH OFFICE

26:08.375 --> 26:11.458
You stay quiet in here.
We'll interrogate you later.

26:11.541 --> 26:12.583
Hey! Wait.

26:13.250 --> 26:14.708
Please.

26:15.916 --> 26:17.083
What about a guard?

26:19.416 --> 26:20.875
Shouldn't you have one?

26:21.458 --> 26:24.291
What? You're scared of ghosts?

26:26.458 --> 26:28.041
That's not it.

26:28.625 --> 26:30.916
Hey, wait! Wait!

26:31.500 --> 26:33.500
Wait! Don't leave me alone!

27:09.750 --> 27:10.916
Let's go.

27:25.833 --> 27:26.875
108

27:35.458 --> 27:38.416
We're from the Police Bureau.
Your chief knows we're coming.

27:42.208 --> 27:43.958
Seems like they took the bait.

27:44.541 --> 27:46.333
-Huh?
-What's your name, young man?

27:48.041 --> 27:49.708
I'm Shinnosuke Sayama.

27:49.791 --> 27:51.916
Shinnosuke, hold these for me.

27:52.000 --> 27:53.041
Huh?

27:53.625 --> 27:54.708
Wait!

28:00.416 --> 28:04.375
The time is 2:17 p.m.
Number 108, Shujiro Saga.

28:22.916 --> 28:25.416
We're here to examine the suspect
who was just detained.

28:25.500 --> 28:28.041
Sir, he's in the detention cell
in the basement.

28:28.125 --> 28:29.333
Let me show you the way.

28:37.500 --> 28:38.541
Hello, sir.

28:43.583 --> 28:44.583
Hello.

28:45.458 --> 28:47.458
I'll join them for the examination.

28:48.041 --> 28:48.875
Yes, sir.

29:44.375 --> 29:45.833
Isn't this place…

30:10.125 --> 30:14.333
At 2:17 p.m. by Kuwana-juku,
number 108, Shujiro Saga was eliminated.

32:02.000 --> 32:05.625
MITSUI BANK
RECORD OF ALL TRANSACTIONS

32:05.708 --> 32:07.833
MITSUI BANK
OPENING LOAN AND DEPOSIT LEDGER

32:08.333 --> 32:10.208
MITSUI BANK GUIDELINES
FOR ESTIMATING WRITE-OFFS

32:10.291 --> 32:12.041
MITSUI BANK
INTERNAL RULES

32:19.250 --> 32:20.625
This place is…

32:29.791 --> 32:31.041
MITSUI BANK

32:31.125 --> 32:32.333
A bank.

32:42.000 --> 32:43.166
That guy…

33:12.375 --> 33:13.833
Are you here to interrogate me?

33:15.041 --> 33:16.041
Listen to me.

33:16.916 --> 33:20.583
I didn't kill anybody.
I can explain everything.

33:21.166 --> 33:23.958
Some crazy people
ordered us to kill each other.

33:24.041 --> 33:26.000
They threatened to kill us if we escaped.

33:26.083 --> 33:28.708
Put me under police protection.

33:29.291 --> 33:32.291
Please. Keep the Kodoku away from me…

33:40.250 --> 33:41.625
What's going on?

33:41.708 --> 33:42.750
Wait! No, wait--

34:51.041 --> 34:52.666
So 108's body is in here?

34:52.750 --> 34:53.666
Yes, sir.

35:28.583 --> 35:30.916
Seems that a rat has slipped inside.

35:43.458 --> 35:45.291
Who's there?

35:49.708 --> 35:52.291
I'm Takayama
of the Police Bureau's Fourth Division.

35:55.041 --> 35:58.291
I don't recall any subordinates
with that name.

35:59.250 --> 36:02.583
Oh, you're from the Police Bureau too…

36:04.375 --> 36:06.125
You're not fooling anyone.

36:09.041 --> 36:10.375
Kyojin Tsuge.

36:47.541 --> 36:49.708
Do you really think you can escape?

36:51.541 --> 36:52.500
Come now.

36:54.041 --> 36:55.916
Don't waste time and show yourself.

37:01.083 --> 37:02.583
Kokushu Saga.

37:17.041 --> 37:18.500
Hanjiro Nakamura.

37:19.583 --> 37:21.416
Please, call me Sakura now.

37:22.708 --> 37:25.083
I saw how Ando was cut down
at Tenryuji Temple.

37:25.583 --> 37:27.125
I suspected it was you.

37:27.208 --> 37:30.083
I've been secretly rooting for you.

37:30.166 --> 37:32.500
I thought you died that day.

37:38.791 --> 37:42.833
Life is unpredictable, isn't it?

37:46.166 --> 37:47.083
I…

37:48.458 --> 37:50.666
I have always looked up to you.

37:52.333 --> 37:54.083
Just tell me one thing.

37:56.375 --> 37:58.625
What is it that you are trying to achieve?

38:01.083 --> 38:02.916
I cannot answer that.

38:06.125 --> 38:10.708
When two old friends reunite,
they either share drinks together…

38:13.458 --> 38:14.750
or they kill each other.

38:18.000 --> 38:19.375
It's one or the other.

39:31.708 --> 39:36.375
Our analysis shows that the location
they were sending the coded telegrams to

39:36.458 --> 39:38.500
was the Nihonbashi Telegraph Office.

39:39.000 --> 39:44.250
So we tracked the individual
who picked up the telegrams…

39:45.625 --> 39:47.541
and found out where they went.

39:49.541 --> 39:50.541
Where?

39:51.833 --> 39:53.708
The final destination…

39:57.000 --> 39:58.958
was the Home Ministry's Police Bureau.

40:15.375 --> 40:18.666
Gentlemen.
Apologies for keeping you waiting.

40:19.250 --> 40:20.875
We've been waiting for you, sir.

40:23.041 --> 40:25.208
It took you rather long, Organizer.

40:25.291 --> 40:26.291
Indeed.

40:47.208 --> 40:48.291
Home Minister.

40:49.041 --> 40:51.916
I cannot be sure if I should say this…

40:56.000 --> 40:57.083
What is it?

40:59.458 --> 41:01.791
Can we really trust Kawaji?

41:09.500 --> 41:14.166
Once again, I would like to thank you all
for agreeing to this game.

41:16.375 --> 41:18.625
It's all for the good of this country.

41:19.125 --> 41:21.416
If it's money you need, don't hesitate.

41:21.500 --> 41:23.041
Thank you very much.

41:26.708 --> 41:30.291
Eradicating the specters
is a huge project for our nation.

41:31.125 --> 41:33.208
A great cause
that we cannot afford to fail.

41:35.083 --> 41:40.000
Let us be the ones
to fulfill this duty, shall we?

41:57.708 --> 42:00.958
For the future of this country.

42:21.583 --> 42:26.583
70 REMAINING

46:21.416 --> 46:24.916
Subtitle translation by: Daisy Savage
